{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter019-001","severity":"P1","label":"Rebuild-commit fan-out re-derives to 2,073 billed min/day from the 13 medians, but only 9 of the 13 downstream workflows can take a paths-ignore key; the 4 that already declare paths: need a negated entry inside paths because GitHub forbids both keys on one event.","iteration":19,"sources":["specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/scratch/ci-run-data/summary.md",".github/workflows/trigger-index-rebuild.yml",".github/workflows/spec-kit-check.yml",".github/workflows/hooks-node-tests.yml",".github/workflows/opencode-plugin-tests.yml",".github/workflows/markdown-link-integrity.yml"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter019-002","severity":"P1","label":"No downstream CI job reads the generated index content: the only test naming the four committed paths asserts the rebuild workflow's staged set from the YAML, and the index suite generates into a temp out/ dir, so excluding spec-kit-check from rebuild commits costs no index coverage.","iteration":19,"sources":[".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/trigger-index-rebuild-workflow.vitest.ts",".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/trigger-index.vitest.ts",".github/workflows/trigger-index-rebuild.yml"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter019-003","severity":"P2","label":"F18-4's derivation does not reproduce but its figure is a floor: one merged job of 13 jobs keeps one checkout, leaving 153-465 s = 3-8 billed minutes against 25 today, a saving of 17-22 min/push (1,241-1,606/day) not 10-12.","iteration":19,"sources":["specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/scratch/ci-run-data/summary.md","specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/research/iterations/iteration-004.md","specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/research/iterations/iteration-018.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter019-004","severity":"P2","label":"Iteration 001's claim that merging jobs cannot recover the per-job ceiling is false; billing is per job, so consolidation removes 12 ceilings, and the ~986 min/day ceiling waste is a property of the job graph that sits inside F18-4's saving rather than a separate lever.","iteration":19,"sources":["specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/scratch/ci-run-data/summary.md","specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/research/iterations/iteration-001.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter019-005","severity":"P2","label":"The tree-cache 145 min/day and the hooks-into-plugin merge 124 min/day are not additive: with the cache the merged job is 189 s = 4 billed vs 5, so the pair is ~207/day and summing them double-counts one provision.","iteration":19,"sources":["specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/research/iterations/iteration-003.md","specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/research/iterations/iteration-012.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter019-006","severity":"P3","label":"playbook-operator-contract's 'deliberately NOT path-filtered' comment reads as a veto of the generated-path ignore and must be amended in the same change, although the ignore is compatible with its rationale.","iteration":19,"sources":[".github/workflows/playbook-operator-contract.yml"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter019-007","severity":"P3","label":"The 776 s CLI vitest project is the only lever inside spec-kit-check that crosses a billing boundary for a small change: 1,215 s bills 21, at or below 1,200 s bills 20, so a 15 s trim is worth ~50 min/day and anything smaller buys wall-clock only.","iteration":19,"sources":["specs/system-speckit/053-ci-workflow-efficiency/001-research/scratch/ci-run-data/summary.md",".github/workflows/spec-kit-check.yml"]}
